<title>NEW ZEALAND: Foreign share of NZ govt securities 57.1 in Jan.</title>
<headline>Foreign share of NZ govt securities 57.1 in Jan.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The proportion of New Zealand government securities held by foreigners rose in January to 57.1 percent from 55.5 percent in December, the Reserve Bank said on Thursday.  </p>
<p>Survey of non-resident holders:</p>
<p>			   Jan 1997	    Dec 1996	   Jan 1996</p>
<p>Bills &amp; Bonds</p>
<p>		 Value  Pct(*)	Value  Pct(*)    Value  Pct(*)</p>
<p>T-Bills	    3,455.5   44.0    3,510.7  41.1   4,623.0  64.0</p>
<p>Govt Bonds	11,366.7   62.8   11,375.3  62.2   7,855.8  41.5</p>
<p>Total Secs	14,822.2   57.1   14,886.0  55.5  12,478.8  47.7</p>
<p>Benchmark Bonds</p>
<p>	07/97	  604.1   33.7	877.0  44.7     605.5  30.9</p>
<p>	07/98	1,641.9   67.0    1,603.9  65.5   1,099.5  44.9</p>
<p>	02/00	2,017.1   67.0    1,790.5  59.5     988.5  32.8</p>
<p>	02/01	1,237.3   61.9    1,515.2  75.8     404.5  43.7</p>
<p>	03/02	1,650.5   65.7    1,496.0  59.6   1,113.4  44.3</p>
<p>	04/04	2,032.7   66.8    1,864.3  61.2   1,481.1  48.7</p>
<p>	11/06	2,027.0   73.0    2,079.0  74.9   1,154.6  54.9</p>
<p>	02/16	  156.1   36.1	149.4  34.6</p>
<p>(*) percentage's represent non-resident holding as a percent of total securities in market.</p>
<p>-- Wellington newsroom 64 4 4734 746</p>
</text>
